{"time": "20261117T171927Z", "think": "Ask to see keep.", "command": "say 1", "result": "Sakeeus-Wan: Sakeeus-Wan, wall captain, at the gatehouse. Tells: a Toh-Wo may sleep in the barracks; the keep is shut to strangers while three Sarpa raiders rob the chalk carts on the western approach and he needs every spear on the walls; kill those three and he will open the keep and pay a hundred gold. Checks: nothing. Does: sets stage 15.\n\n*** Journal updated: The Cellar Door ***\nJournal: The wall captain, Sakeeus-Wan, says a Toh-Wo may sleep in the barracks, but the keep stays shut to strangers while three Sarpa raiders rob the chalk carts on the western approach. I'm to kill the three raiders; then he will open the keep and pay me. I can still go in unseen by the trapdoor in the yard instead.\nObjective: Kill the three Sarpa raiders on Fort Chalkmoth's western approach. (marker: Sarpa Raider, Sarpa Raider, Sarpa Raider)\nObjective: Tell the wall captain the raiders are dead. (marker: Sakeeus-Wan)\n\nThe game pauses. Answer these four questions from what the game has shown you, in your own words, numbered, in one command: answer '1. ... 2. ... 3. ... 4. ...'\n1. What is going on? (who you work for, what has happened, why it matters, as far as you know)\n2. What are you expected to do next, and where?\n3. What options do you have for doing it? (the ways through you can see, and any choice in front of you)\n4. Is there any word, name, person or thing you do not understand? Do you know how you could find out?", "summary": {"stage": 15, "at": "fort-chalkmoth", "items": {"item.lockpick": 2, "thing.mn.unbound-note": 1, "item.mn05.voh-vastei-armour": 1, "thing.mn.eye-setting": 1, "thing.mn.keystone": 1, "thing.mn.grave-stake": 1, "thing.mn.paralysis-poison": 3, "thing.mn.bronze-disc": 1, "thing.mn.parchment-map": 1, "thing.mn10.rapier": 1}, "gold": 1050, "flags": {"flag.mn03.truth": true, "flag.mn06.note-read": true, "flag.mn06.done": true, "flag.main.seal-question": true, "fla