{"time": "20261117T171955Z", "think": "Check state after reading.", "command": "journal", "result": "The Cellar Door\n- Never-Writes-Twice says Fort Chalkmoth is a fort like any other, but a wounded Unbound scout told me to ask what moans in its cellar. This is my own errand, not the order's; the hunt waits at Bell Station and either may come first. Fort Chalkmoth is the Archwardens' fort on the Chixathe Mesa above Noota Nara. I'm to get into the fort and see its cellar: the wall captain at the gate may let me in, or I may find another way in unseen.\n- The wall captain, Sakeeus-Wan, says a Toh-Wo may sleep in the barracks, but the keep stays shut to strangers while three Sarpa raiders rob the chalk carts on the western approach. I'm to kill the three raiders; then he will open the keep and pay me. I can still go in unseen by the trapdoor in the yard instead.\n- I came up through the trapdoor in the yard into the cellar's guardroom, unseen. If the garrison sees me in here, they will attack. The stair from the guardroom climbs to the quartermaster's store. I'm to see what I can of the cellar: the store above, the gaoler at the stair's foot and the inner door.\nObjective: Look at the stack of sap jars by the stair in the quartermaster's store.\nObjective: Speak to the gaoler at the foot of the cellar stair.\nObjective: Try the cellar door.\nMarker 1: Stack of Sap Jars (Jal-Veesa Knot), at Quartermaster's Store\nMarker 2: Tsleel-Vaku, at Fort Chalkmoth Guardroom\nMarker 3: Door to Cellar Door, at Fort Chalkmoth Guardroom\nYou carry: Lockpick x2, Unbound-Note, Voh-Vastei-Armour, Eye-Setting, Keystone, Grave-Stake, Paralysis-Poison x3, Bronze-Disc, Parchment-Map, Rapier; 1050 gold.", "summary": {"stage": 25, "at": "Quartermaster's Store", "items": {"item.lockpick": 2, "thing.mn.unbound-note": 1, "item.mn05.voh-vastei-armour": 1, "thing.mn.eye-setting": 1, "thing.mn.keystone": 1, "thing.mn.grave-stake": 1, "thing.mn.paralysis-poison": 3, "thing.mn.bronze-disc": 1, "thing.